#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100733 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101021 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86221215-32a6-5c5a-bcd7-220e166bcee8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Points That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "a0f21b4c-0f5c-5567-aaec-9da481d2e7ac" :question/math-academy-id "e-547" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x) = x^2-2x+2$ on the interval $[0,3].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       f(c) (b-a)  & =  \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n              f(c)    & = \\dfrac {1}{b-a} \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n    & = \\dfrac {1}{3-0} \\int_0^3  (x^2-2x+2) \\, \\textrm dx \\[5pt]\n     & =  \\left . \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot  \\left[\\dfrac{x^3}{3} -x^2 +2x\\right] \\right|_0^3 \\[5pt]\n    & =   \\dfrac {1}{3} \\cdot \\left[ \\left(\\dfrac{3^3}{3} -3^2 +2\\cdot3\\right) -  \\left(\\dfrac{0^3}{3} -0^2 +2\\cdot0\\right)\\right] \\[5pt]\n    & =  \\dfrac {1}{3}\\cdot6 \\[5pt]\n    &  = 2.\n}\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ {c}^{2}-2c+2 & =2 \\\\ c(c-2) & =0 \\\\ c & =0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100734 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "0c84fc6d-422e-5729-94d2-a12cda71f78d" :question/math-academy-id "e-548" :question/problem "Find the average value of the function $f(x) = x - 2$ on the interval $[-2, 4].$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}x-2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x){|}_{-2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-2(4))-(\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}-2(-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[(8-8)-(2+4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-6) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100735 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "244bb10c-4c6f-5be0-bd9a-72b4defee245" :question/math-academy-id "e-549" :question/problem "Find $c$ such that the average value of $g(x) = 3 x$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $3.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(\\frac{3{c}^{2}}{2}-0) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{3c}{2} \\\\ c & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100736 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "a1572338-79f7-5da7-b9f6-552dcb7984a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-550" :question/problem "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](images/64/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval is\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, we see that\n\n$$\n\\int_{1}^{6} f(x)\\: \\textrm{d}x = -5 + 2 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo, applying the average value formula, we find that the average value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-1}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a93b98b3-fc61-5f38-b2cf-0e4d0d84697e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098936} {:answer/id #uuid "15bf6613-ed49-5c14-8962-302fba899942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098937} {:answer/id #uuid "2553718f-9dc9-58d5-b044-7b0ec9b75acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098938} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5c77a9-0ae1-5fca-9298-b1a2fbddfb48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098939} {:answer/id #uuid "70c7b215-8a02-5ef3-8a75-f44389330a1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098940}] :answer-field/id #uuid "76405eb1-2f74-542e-aab9-001fe5ee76ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098935}] :question/id #uuid "794367ad-cee9-50fc-b4cc-e78beb478cad" :question/math-academy-id "q-18144" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d661fd02727800f40ccaaf7f388b99b61b9e3a2d6c2da351c47b2166d1182b48.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x)$, which is defined on $[- 3, 6]$, is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $40$, $20$ and $10$, respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[- 3, 6]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101023 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bedcde-cbc1-5634-8846-eb58ffda32e2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Interval Given the Average Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e2aa02f-a4ec-550a-ade8-9e48bb5f1850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295716} {:answer/id #uuid "59648138-a114-51e5-892e-a0c2df92248a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295782} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe67af0-fcaf-5d5e-a56d-77eb12803f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296359} {:answer/id #uuid "d38fcd7d-c6b8-55d1-8fad-9a37e56de360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296381} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2eab6a-2a27-5e35-9dc7-aaca0c578fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59648138-a114-51e5-892e-a0c2df92248a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295782} :answer-field/id #uuid "6374f584-b639-5c44-b777-84bde5e5310d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16b1bc24-13e7-5da4-a569-33e3816b732d" :question/math-academy-id "q-30872" :question/problem "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101024 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd9167b4-572f-589f-9b94-b62ba57eb28f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4f22f82-3f4c-56a7-8fca-b1699296b03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f22f82-3f4c-56a7-8fca-b1699296b03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296486} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5ebfc2e-32f9-5714-a71a-21c80776c9ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e5a2c9b-15eb-580e-9b48-bc6a0c515d66" :question/math-academy-id "q-316309" :question/problem "![](images/1c/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d4f785-6f5a-5ce0-bf69-39aad915511d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{56.5}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302796} {:answer/id #uuid "45450f39-4901-5335-a3d0-7f1c044bd30e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{52.1}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302890} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1d0fe5-2d24-59ed-9880-fe68d2d0d545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61.2}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302923} {:answer/id #uuid "559548da-50f2-521b-9452-7fc3e2890a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{50.0}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302984} {:answer/id #uuid "782842d2-e11d-5027-8038-91cd35485b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782842d2-e11d-5027-8038-91cd35485b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58.9}^{∘}F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303198} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fac5b99-d1c6-5e15-afc2-0e7b3ba2570b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2e55b4cb-6c56-5cac-893d-482f84ce6bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-3289" :question/problem "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." :question/worked-solution "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101022 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55fab3ac-cad3-54bd-b07b-9159554b634c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Average Value of a Function Over a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34272274-e39f-56d1-b23d-d6f2a622e4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302781} {:answer/id #uuid "4e6335c6-35ae-5399-8646-8a48ae96cd75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302948} {:answer/id #uuid "cedccea5-0ac5-5eb1-b565-b46dfdb1b62d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303733} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f569b4-3616-56ca-b69b-687f426d0093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303884} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4dab3d-a51f-5405-a9a9-031ff453e188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4dab3d-a51f-5405-a9a9-031ff453e188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304056} :answer-field/id #uuid "08f23813-1ba2-570a-ae16-39c39c5747d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24f38454-bd1c-55d7-83bd-a807c36fe3b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-3297" :question/problem "Within  the interval $[0,\\pi ]$, determine the average value of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi -0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\pi ))-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(-2\\cdot (-1)+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)-(-2\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }[(\\frac{5}{2})-(-\\frac{3}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
